"version\nbuild 485 date 20261030 time 183514\nPureMetal Forge - Anvil, the Raspberry Pi 4 monitor. Version 2.0,\n64-bit AArch64, running with no operating system underneath it.\n  This is build 485 of this board's monitor, made 2026-10-30 at 18:35:14.\n  The number is raised by one by every successful build, so two images\n  can be told apart from the prompt. It says WHICH build this is, not\n  WHAT is in it - a number can be reset, frozen, or carried by a source\n  somebody edited without rebuilding. The digest below is what is in it.\n  This monitor's own image is 6811132 bytes, 00200000 .. 0087EDFB.\n  That extent is the RUNNING IMAGE's own: the compiler marks the end\n  of the image with a symbol and this program reads it, so the length\n  is of the code that is executing and not of a file on a disk that\n  may since have been replaced. It is also why this monitor has no\n  maximum size - type map.\n  That size and the build number above are enough to tell two images\n  apart. For the digest that says WHAT is in it, type:\n    version full        - or crc32 00200000 0067EDFC\n  It is not done here unasked because it reads every byte of the\n  image, which is not instant on a board with its caches off.\n  Built by PureMetal Forge for target pi4.\n  This image is a kernel8.img. The firmware loads the whole file to\n  00200000 and enters it there, with no loader in between -\n  which is why its size is not capped by anything: there is nothing\n  above it in the boot path to make room for.\n  The compiler and linker versions are not stamped into the image, so -\n  unlike U-Boot's version - they are not printed here rather than\n  guessed at.\n  Type info for the board, revision and clocks, or help for the commands.\npmf> "